## Test Smell Audit — Academic testsmells.org 19-Smell Catalog

**Framework:** MSTest 4.x (.NET 10) · **Scope:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests` (1 class, 7 tests)  
**Integration calibration applied:** Class is marked `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 2           | 2              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Smell:** Control-flow (`if`/`else`) inside a test method changes which assertions execute.  
**Affected:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** Only one branch ever executes per run. If the type hierarchy changes, the other path is silently untested — a hidden gap.  
**Fix:** Split into two deterministic tests:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — 50% of behavior is never verified in any given run.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Smell:** Test exercises production code but makes no assertions.  
**Affected:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Problem:** If `Insert` silently corrupts data or inserts partial records, this test still passes. It provides only "no unhandled exception" confidence.  
**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False pass — coverage metrics look healthy but nothing is actually verified.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Sleepy Test

**Smell:** `Thread.Sleep` introduces a hard-coded 3-second wait.  
**Affected:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Calibration note:** Downgraded from High → Medium because this is an integration test where async coordination is sometimes necessary. However, a fixed 3 s sleep is still fragile (too short on slow CI, too long for fast machines).  
**Fix:** Use a polling/retry helper:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await PollUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI; unnecessary 3 s penalty on every run.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Smell:** Multiple assertions without descriptive messages — when one fails, the failure message is ambiguous.  
**Affected:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Detection threshold:** 3+ assertions with no message parameter (this has 4).  
**Fix:** Add the optional message argument:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should be persisted");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should be persisted");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower diagnosis when assertions fail — developers must read source to locate the failure.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

| Test | What's Good |
|------|-------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clean Arrange-Act-Assert; only 2 assertions (below roulette threshold) |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single focused assertion; clear negative-case verification |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count `3` is self-documenting (added 3 items); uses `CollectionAssert` |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Legitimate integration scenario; single clear assertion |

The fixture design is also clean — `_connection` and `_repository` are used by **all** tests, so no General Fixture smell applies.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Impact |
|----------|-------|-----------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Low (add one assertion) | Eliminates a false-pass test |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Medium (split into 2 tests) | Removes hidden untested path |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Medium (add poll helper) | Eliminates flakiness + speeds suite |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Low (add message strings) | Improves debuggability |

**Bottom line:** 3 of 7 tests are healthy and well-structured. The remaining 4 have real but fixable issues — priorities 1 and 2 are the most critical because they mask bugs that would otherwise go undetected.
